diff --git a/docs/agents/source-map.md b/docs/agents/source-map.md
index 9c4e739..ba6fa38 100644
--- a/docs/agents/source-map.md
+++ b/docs/agents/source-map.md
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ Page files are checked by the build's boot check (`lib/page-boot.mjs`): the asse
 - R2 (`system-core.js` `SYSTEM`; crate `sv-system`; reference `SYSTEM_JS`): the system itself (validate, id, size, one running system) is Rust; `SYSTEM.facts` and `selftest` stay in the JS wrapper because facts drives the Reader engine (`sigmaPeek`, `priceHistory`, `episodeGroups`, frozen until the episode-outcomes run) and moves with it in R6. `sv-system` is a plain API (`System::new(def, opt)`, `step(&Snap) -> Vec<Intent>`, `filled`, `closed`, `cancelled`, `end`, `force`, `state`; `Snap` is the snapshot a second), so the R3 runner can own instances inside Rust; `ops.rs` is the JSON layer with a `Handles<System>` registry (`system_create` returns a handle, every call takes it). `create()` returns the same object as before plus `dispose()` (the page frees by `FinalizationRegistry` too; the offline harness calls it). Load-time ids: `runner.js` (`TR_DEF`) and `trader-view.js` (`TV_SYS`) fill from `SYSTEM.id` in `SVWASM.ready.then`. Inputs cross as JSON, so `-0` in a snapshot arrives as 0 (sign of a zero in a reading only). Size work: `opt-level = "z"`, one shared `sv_core::sort_by` (the std sort was compiled per type). `design-harness.mjs` gives its vm contexts `SVWASM` (`coreContext`). `node parity.mjs system [--designs N] [--all-sessions]` (`lib/parity-system.mjs`: a dual system runs both versions and compares every call and every state; self-test, validate/id, random systems on random streams, the saved sessions before 2026-11-16 using the cached snapshots).
 - R3 (`runner-core.js` `RUNNER`; crate `sv-runner`; reference `RUNNER_JS`, which runs `SYSTEM_JS`): the stepping runs in Rust. A `Runner` owns its 7 `System`s and their 20 twins each (sv-system's plain API, no JSON between them), so `step(snap)` is ONE call for every instance (R2 crossed the boundary per instance: about 1.4 ms per instance-second, the harness 28x slower than JS; now about 0.05 ms for all 147 instances, faster than the JS reference). The twins' mulberry32 / FNV-1a is ported bit for bit (u32 wrapping ops). Rows are built as `sv_core::obj::Obj` (a flat object with keys in the JS literal's order, one shared serializer) so journal rows keep their key order. `ops.rs`: `runner_create/step/interrupt/move/state/risk/drop` over a `Handles<Runner>`; `Snap` gained `q` (the quote the runner fills at). Stays in JS in the wrapper: reading the starting journal (equity per system and twin, interrupted positions: `fresh()`), `carryOf`, `driver` (gap rule, carry, stage moves; it disposes the runner it replaces), `evaluate` (folds over JS row objects; shipping all rows through JSON would cost more than it saves) and the `runner:*` self-test (runs on WASM). `create()` returns the same object plus `dispose()`. Rows come back as JSON, so a non-finite number is null. `TRN.ready` also waits for `SVWASM.ready` (a run begins only after it). `node parity.mjs runner [--all-sessions] [--only-real]` (`lib/parity-runner.mjs`): self-test on both, random configurations (systems, twins, fee, cap, seed, stages, a handed-over journal, moves, interrupts, driver gaps), the saved sessions before 2026-11-16 on the cached snapshots (defaults with the harness's carried journal, and a random configuration), comparing every row, state, risk, journal and evaluate. Known edge: `SYSTEM.state()` (R2) leaves `trigger.lastEnter.region.hi/lo` as null where the JS had NaN; `RUNNER.state()` restores the NaN.
 - R4 (`exec-core.js` `EXEC`; crate `sv-exec`; reference `EXEC_JS`): the demo-execution machine (create / onRow / reply / tick / start / poll / kill / drain / state / snapshot, requests, mirror rows, faults) is Rust, one machine per handle. SAFETY: the base-URL rule (`is_demo_base`: the demo host or `http://127.0.0.1|localhost:<2-5 digits>`; `ALLOW_LIVE` a `const false`) is in Rust, `send` queues nothing for a machine that is not allowed, and the wrapper keeps a second copy of the host test (`jsDemo`): `create` throws if the two disagree and `drain` hands out no request from a machine that is not allowed; `isDemoBase` is false until the module is loaded; `exec.js` makes no machine before `SVWASM.loaded`. `merge`, the self-test and its fake exchange stay JS (merge reshapes arbitrary journal rows by reference and key order). `node parity.mjs exec`: self-test calls, the guard on look-alike and mutated hosts, random sequences on a fake exchange, real journals before 2026-11-16 (`lib/parity-exec.mjs`); the edge differences are listed at the top of `exec-core.js`. Rust unit tests: `cargo test -p sv-exec` (guard, no request when not allowed).
+- R5 (`market-core.js` `MARKET`, `chunk-core.js` `CHUNK`, `micro-core.js` `MICRO`; crate `sv-feed`; references `MARKET_JS`, `CHUNK_JS`): the rule here is per-call cost, because these sit on the per-input path and one JSON call across the boundary costs about 5 us (a 1000-level book about 350 us to send, more than the JS needs to process it). Measured on run 20261112041209 (`node parity.mjs bench`: 17 inputs/s of trades, 13 quotes, 3 books, 4 timer ticks): `MARKET.stampMid`/`bumpCvd` (per trade, 0.05 us in JS), `CHUNK.pipeline.input`/`thinner`/`timeOf` (per input, 0.1 us), `replay` and `firstDiff` (need the JS engine and row objects), `MARKET.prune` (moves arrays), `cvdRow` and the `fresh*` constants (no logic) and ALL of `MICRO` (`sample` 400 us, `bnTopN` 110 us, `bnSweepFeed` per trade) stay JS. Ported: `MARKET.midRow` (4/s: the rule runs in Rust, the wrapper builds `{t, bn, hl}`; falls back to the same rule in JS until the module is loaded), `CHUNK.check`, `fileName` (once per chunk, throws RangeError for an invalid time) and `leftRunning` (2 s timer; only the fields the rule reads cross, the wrapper builds the item objects in key order because `serde_json` without `preserve_order` sorts keys). Cost of the port: +31 us/s (midRow) and +7 us/s (leftRunning), nothing measurable on the page; wasm +11.7 KB (inputs and outputs are read as `serde_json::Value` by hand: derived structs cost 27 KB). No worker uses these cores. `run-record.js` `rrLeft` waits for `SVWASM.loaded`. `design-harness.mjs` gives `CHUNK` a wasm context. `node parity.mjs micro|market|chunk|bench` (`lib/parity-feed.mjs`: both self-tests, random calls, every recorded chunk name and run before 2026-11-16, and the three recorded runs replayed through both pipelines: identical cuts and chunk bytes, equal to the recording; `micro` only self-tests). Edge differences (inputs the page never sends): `midRow` with a string or `Infinity` quote reads as no quote; `leftRunning` with a non-string `disk.tone` or a missing `battery.level` differs; `fileName` reads `startedAt` as a number.
 - `parity.mjs <core>` (root): replays the self-test's calls and seeded random inputs through both versions, plus real journals, comparing with `Object.is`; one line per batch.
 
